    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d574">

                <pb facs="0474" n="462" xml:id="pg462"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00112 European War 1939/5436: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé at Tangier</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-05-11T20:00:00+01:00">May 11, 1942—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 11—2:51 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>214. My 195, May 5, 8 p.m. Following repeated inquiries High Commissariat has now
                    telephoned to state that reference in the second paragraph of General Orgaz’
                    note is to the interview had on April 11.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Madrid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
